// resolver-modules-2 : a `P :: import` namespace alias reaching a member that does
// not exist AT ALL must fire R2007, the same answer the unqualified form gives —
// and it must fire from inside a `match` arm, which is where the silence bit.
//
// Two silences stacked before the fix. `namespace_member_type` returned
// `TY_UNRESOLVED` without a diagnostic for an ABSENT member (it only reported the
// PRIVATE case, R2008), and `pattern_type_of` lowered arm patterns into a throwaway
// sink, so anything it did raise was dropped. The pattern then interned as `ref _`,
// which matches every erased value under the VM but nothing native: the same `match`
// took a different arm depending on the backend, silently. Four arms in `vader/vm`
// and `vader/c_emit` lived that way for months.
module "snippet"

L :: import "snippet/lib"

main :: fn() -> i32 {
    v: L.Either = L.Real { .n = 1 }
    return match v {
        is L.Absent -> 2
        is L.Real   -> 1
        is L.Other  -> 3
    }
}
